  "id": "supervision",
  "term": "supervision",
  "definition": "In counselling and psychotherapy, supervision is a professional support and oversight process for trainees or therapists. It is generally seen as helpful for supervisees and is associated with factors such as self-awareness, self-efficacy, and the supervisory working alliance, although evidence about its effects on patients and any one best supervision model is limited.",
